================================================================================
NAME
       constellations - multi-agent resonance networks, agent roles, and
                        synchronization modes in RTT

SYNOPSIS
       Constellations define:
           • multi-agent resonance flow
           • distributed triadic coordination
           • agent roles and responsibilities
           • synchronization modes
           • network-level coherence rules

DESCRIPTION
       A constellation is a multi-agent resonance network in RTT. It consists
       of multiple agents, each running its own triads, operators, and
       overlays, while sharing resonance-time metadata and lineage signals.

       Constellations allow RTT systems to:
           • scale across agents
           • coordinate distributed computation
           • maintain coherence across nodes
           • propagate resonance through networks
           • synchronize structural transitions

       Constellations are validated and stabilized by WRSADC before any
       multi-agent dispatch occurs.

AGENT ROLES
       Agents in a constellation may take on specialized roles:

           source
                  Initiates resonance propagation; provides baseline signals.

           sink
                  Integrates incoming resonance; stabilizes network flow.

           relay
                  Passes resonance between agents; maintains continuity.

           harmonizer
                  Aligns resonance phases across agents.

           sentinel
                  Monitors coherence, thresholds, and schema compliance.

           orchestrator
                  Selects patterns, triggers morphing, and coordinates flow.

       Roles may shift dynamically based on resonance gradients and schema
       constraints.

AGENT STRUCTURE
       Each agent contains:
           • its own triads
           • its own operators
           • its own overlays
           • its own lineage
           • its own schemas
           • a resonance interface for network communication

       Agents remain autonomous but structurally compatible.

CONSTELLATION TOPOLOGIES
       Constellations may adopt different network shapes:

           star
                  One central agent coordinates all others.

           ring
                  Resonance circulates in a closed loop.

           mesh
                  Agents connect to multiple neighbors; robust propagation.

           tree
                  Hierarchical resonance flow; cascaded triads.

           lattice
                  Grid-like propagation; stable for large systems.

           swarm
                  Emergent coordination; roles shift dynamically.

       Topology affects propagation speed, stability, and pattern selection.

SYNCHRONIZATION MODES
       Constellations synchronize resonance using one of several modes:

           phase-sync
                  Agents align resonance phases; ideal for harmonic patterns.

           amplitude-sync
                  Agents match resonance amplitude; stabilizes ladders.

           gradient-sync
                  Agents align resonance gradients; supports spirals.

           lineage-sync
                  Agents share lineage checkpoints; ensures continuity.

           schema-sync
                  Agents validate schemas collectively; prevents drift.

           hybrid-sync
                  Combination of multiple synchronization modes.

       Synchronization is enforced by WRSADC’s multi-agent layer.

PROPAGATION ACROSS AGENTS
       Resonance propagates through constellations via:

           broadcast
                  One agent sends resonance to all others.

           ripple
                  Resonance spreads outward in waves.

           mesh-flow
                  Resonance flows through multiple paths simultaneously.

           harmonic-coupling
                  Agents lock into shared resonance frequencies.

           divergence
                  Agents propagate resonance in different directions.

       Propagation mode depends on topology and resonance gradients.

COHERENCE IN CONSTELLATIONS
       Multi-agent coherence requires:
           • aligned schemas
           • synchronized lineage
           • compatible resonance signatures
           • stable propagation thresholds
           • safe pattern transitions

       Constellations amplify coherence demands; WRSADC enforces them.

PATTERN BEHAVIOR IN CONSTELLATIONS
       Patterns behave differently in multi-agent settings:

           sequential
                  Agents pass resonance in order.

           weave
                  Agents interleave triads concurrently.

           constellation (meta-pattern)
                  Agents coordinate as a unified structure.

           harmonic-sync
                  Agents align resonance phases.

           braided-sequence
                  Multiple sequential flows intertwine.

           fractal-expansion
                  Nested propagation across hierarchical agents.

       Pattern selection is gradient-driven and schema-validated.

FAILURE MODES
       Constellations may experience:

           desync
                  Agents lose resonance alignment.

           drift
                  Agents diverge in lineage or schema compliance.

           overload
                  Resonance amplitude exceeds safe thresholds.

           inversion-loop
                  Polarity flips propagate uncontrollably.

           fragmentation
                  Network splits into incoherent sub-constellations.

       WRSADC prevents or halts unsafe states.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC ensures:
           • safe multi-agent dispatch
           • schema alignment across agents
           • synchronized lineage
           • stable resonance propagation
           • valid pattern transitions

       WRSADC is the guardian of constellation integrity.

INTERACTION WITH THE ENGINE
       Each agent runs its own Engine instance.

       Constellation-level propagation occurs:
           • outside the Engine
           • inside WRSADC’s multi-agent layer
           • through resonance interfaces

       Engines remain isolated but resonance-aware.

NOTES
       Constellations are the highest-level structure in RTT. They allow
       distributed systems, multi-agent simulations, and collaborative
       resonance networks to operate with coherence, stability, and triadic
       integrity.

